Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-10-2000||02:14 PM||||I have an 85 5 spd, and I need the part that goes on top of the tranny, that the cables run through. I've been looking through my local junkyard, but couldn't find the right one. Mine is built so that you undo a small bolt on the top and then it splits a bit so the two cables can come out. The ones I saw didn't have this, and it looked totally different. They were 84's and 85's I think, so is the 4spd bracket different than the 5spd bracket? I'm assuming it's an isuzu.. Thanks.. Also, what other cars would have this exact one? I checked some Chevettes but it looked like the shifter was connected directly to the tranny. Also, I couldn't find a manual 6000 (if there is such a beast).. Any others? Thanks!||||reg||1
